From: pogo-bash <pogo-bash@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 19:47:15 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 56/56] LibWeb: a seek inside a buffered range does not lower
 readyState

The playback manager reports only current data while it seeks; readyState is about what is buffered, so a paused seek within the buffered range dropped to HAVE_CURRENT_DATA and came back with a second canplay and canplaythrough, which Chrome does not fire.
---
 Libraries/LibWeb/HTML/HTMLMediaElement.cpp | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Libraries/LibWeb/HTML/HTMLMediaElement.cpp b/Libraries/LibWeb/HTML/HTMLMediaElement.cpp
index a4dbca5395..7cfc94e265 100644
--- a/Libraries/LibWeb/HTML/HTMLMediaElement.cpp
+++ b/Libraries/LibWeb/HTML/HTMLMediaElement.cpp
@@ -2633,6 +2633,14 @@ void HTMLMediaElement::update_ready_state()
     auto current_range = ranges.range_at_or_after(current_time);
     auto available_data = m_playback_manager->available_data();
 
+    // AD-HOC: A seek holds the pipeline at "current data" while it decodes the frame at the new position, but readyState is
+    //         about what is buffered: a seek to a position inside a buffered range that runs past it leaves the element
+    //         able to play on, so it does not drop to HAVE_CURRENT_DATA and come back with a second canplay (Chrome keeps
+    //         HAVE_ENOUGH_DATA through such a seek; HTML's seek algorithm does not lower readyState itself).
+    if (m_seeking && available_data == Media::AvailableData::Current && current_range.has_value()
+        && current_range->start <= current_time && current_range->end > current_time)
+        available_data = Media::AvailableData::Future;
+
     if (available_data == Media::AvailableData::None
         || (available_data == Media::AvailableData::Current && !current_range.has_value())) {
         // 1. Set the HTMLMediaElement's readyState attribute to HAVE_METADATA.
